# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TasteBuddy environment
#
# One of these matters: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Without it the app loads and says it
# is not switched on, because reading a menu is the only thing it does.
#
# Everything else is optional. `npm run dev` works with this file holding
# nothing but that one line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Reading menus ---------------------------------------------------------
# Photographing a menu and looking up a dish both go to Claude.
#
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com → Settings → API keys. Billing has
# to be set up on the account first.
#
# There is no sign-in, so anyone with the address can spend your money. Two
# caps in lib/dish/rate-limit.ts hold it: forty lookups an hour per browser,
# and two thousand a day across everyone. Raise them when there are real people
# using it; the second one is the difference between a busy day and a bill you
# did not choose.
#
# The model says what a dish is *normally* made with, because somebody standing
# in front of a menu they cannot read is asking exactly that, and "pad thai
# usually has peanuts" is the answer that keeps them safe. It has no vocabulary
# for certainty: every answer is "usually" or "sometimes", and every screen
# says the kitchen is the only one who knows.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Pictures of dishes -----------------------------------------------------
# The dish screen draws its own 3D model from the dish's name, and then fetches
# a drawing from pollinations.ai and fades it in over the top. That service is
# free and needs no key or account, so there is nothing to set here to switch
# it on.
#
# Only the dish's name is sent, never anything about the diner, and the request
# goes through this app rather than from the phone. Answers are cached for a
# year by name, so a dish is drawn once for everybody.
#
# It asks for an illustration, never a photograph, and the screen says so. A
# picture is believed faster than a sentence, and nothing here has seen the
# real plate.
# DISH_IMAGES=off                     # 3D model only, no drawings
# DISH_IMAGE_HOST=https://example/    # point it at a different generator

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for exactly one thing: counting lookups, so the caps above hold across
# containers rather than per-process. There is no food and no people in it, and
# what anybody searched for is not recorded. Apply db/schema.sql first.
#
# Leave it unset and the counters live in memory instead. Fine locally; not a
# real limit anywhere else.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/tastebuddy

# Set to `disable` only for a local Postgres with no TLS.
# PGSSLMODE=disable

# Connections per serverless container. Keep this small.
# PGPOOL_MAX=5
